table acts

## Proposed running order

I treated the changeover column as the minutes needed after that act. The interval absorbs the strike after the act before it, so the puppet piece (7 min strike) goes just before the interval. The 16 acts are all in; nothing is cut here.

data order = slot,time,act,performers,length (min),changeover (min); 1,19:30,Welcome and raffle pitch,Margit Halloran-Voss,6,1; 2,19:37,The Mutual Admiration Society (sketch),Pell & Whitcombe,9,4; 3,19:50,"Youth choir, 3 songs",Harbour Street Juniors,12,5; 4,20:07,"Fire-eating (indoor, licensed)",Cass O'Dowd,7,3; 5,20:17,“Moon River” (acoustic),Teodor Beck,5,2; 6,20:24,"Puppet piece (adult, mild language)",Gosforth Marionettes,11,7; Interval,20:35,Interval (puppet strike happens inside it),,20,0; 7,20:55,Aerial silks,Lotte Brandstetter,8,6; 8,21:09,Fog and lasers (tech showcase),Dev Sharma,6,5; 9,21:20,"Stand-up, clean set",Frankie Tan-Ellery,10,1; 10,21:31,Ukulele trio,The Lost Chords,7,3; 11,21:41,Silent auction results,Margit Halloran-Voss,3,0; 12,21:44,Ballad: “I'll Be Seeing You”,Ottoline Park,4,2; 13,21:50,"Poem: “What the River Said, Twice”",Imogen Farouk,4,0; 14,21:54,Tango,Ruiz & Adeyemi,5,2; 15,22:01,"Magic: card tricks, close-up on camera",Harlan Quist,6,2; 16,22:09,Cast sing-along,Whole company,8,0

