## Rule check

table = rule,result,detail; Curtain up 19:30,Pass,slot 1 starts 19:30; Finish by 21:45,Failed,"projected 22:17, 32 min over"; One 20-minute interval,Pass,"20:35 to 20:55, about 65 min in"; Opener and closer fixed,Pass,Welcome is slot 1 and the sing-along is slot 16; Changeover minutes from last column,Pass,all counted except the puppet strike inside the interval; Aerialist not after fog act,Pass,"aerial silks is slot 7, directly after the puppet piece; fog is slot 8"; No two musical acts back to back,Pass,"Moon River, choir, ukulele, ballad and sing-along are never adjacent; tango (recorded music) counted as dance, and it passes either way"; Youth choir on before 20:30,Pass,"on 19:50, off 20:02"

## Watch on the night

- Fire-eating needs 10 minutes' notice for the fire marshal: warn them before 19:57 (act is at 20:07).
- Stand-up will run over if not warned: it is slot 9, so any overrun pushes every later time, and there is no slack before the 21:45 limit anyway.
- The puppet strike (7 min) has to be finished inside the 20-minute interval for the 20:55 restart to hold.

